 "brief_summary": "B2611002 is designed to study how safe and effective an investigational medication (PF-04991532) is in people with Type 2 diabetes. Subjects in the study will receive 1 of 5 treatments for 3 months. One of the treatments will be sitagliptin which is an approved drug, and another treatment will be placebo, which does not contain active ingredient.",
 "eligibility": {
  "criteria": "Inclusion Criteria:\n\nSubjects with type 2 diabetes on stable doses of background medicines for management of diabetes; aged 18-70 years; body mass index between 22.5 and 45.5 kg/m2\n\nExclusion Criteria:\n\nSubjects with type 1 diabetes, heart attack or stroke in the past 6 months, uncontrolled blood pressure, significant kidney disease.",
